    Fix Collab execution in POC and simulation (#5003)
    
    ## What changed
    
    - initialize the server job process `ServerEngine` with its newly
    created communication Cell
    - fail Collab setup cleanly if a server Cell is unavailable
    - propagate simulator `FATAL_SYSTEM_ERROR` state through the simulator
    exit code
    - add focused regression tests for missing Cells and simulator fatal
    status
    
    ## Why
    
    Collab jobs submitted through `PocEnv` synchronized their clients and
    then crashed before setup because `engine.get_cell()` returned `None`.
    The server job process created a Cell but did not initialize its engine
    with it, so `CollabController` failed while calling `get_fqcn()`.
    
    Separately, exceptions raised by `@collab.main` triggered a fatal server
    error but the simulator still returned exit code 0. As a result,
    `recipe.execute()` returned normally and `Run.get_status()` remained
    unavailable in `SimEnv`. The simulator now returns failure when the
    server context records `FATAL_SYSTEM_ERROR`, allowing the existing
    `SimEnv` failure handling to surface the error to the caller.
    
    ## Impact
    
    - Collab jobs can complete in POC deployments.
    - Failed Collab workflows in simulation no longer look successful to the
    calling script.
    
    ## Validation
    
    - `python -m pytest -q tests/unit_test/collab/runtime/controller_test.py
    tests/unit_test/private/fed/app/simulator/simulator_runner_test.py` — 30
    passed
    - `python -m pytest -q tests/unit_test/collab
    tests/unit_test/recipe/sim_env_test.py` — 107 passed
    - Black, isort, and flake8 pass for all changed files
    - shipped `examples/hello-world/hello-collab/job.py` with
    `PocEnv(num_clients=2)` — `FINISHED:COMPLETED`
    - sentinel failing `@collab.main` with `SimEnv` — surfaced as
    `RuntimeError` with simulator return code 2
    
    The full-tree style command also scans generated files under an existing
    `node_modules` directory and reported three unrelated `flatted.py`
    formatting failures; all files changed by this PR pass the scoped
    checks.
